==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Masamune''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Masamune''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Before True Form, Masamune has low stats and a very situational ability. Overall, his first two forms are not recommended unless you have no alternatives, but they still have some use. They can still be used to dish out decent DPS, but not to the level of his True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Masamune increases his usage by raising his stats across the board. He receives more health, allowing him to survive a lot of things more easily. He is also given more range, which is rather significant. Immortal Masamune is rather good for crowd-controlling things like [[Berserkory]] and [[Rain D.]] due to his fast attacks and Knockback ability.

==='''Talents'''===
Date Masamune's talents are not very impressive, and he ends up getting the short end of the stick.

'''Slow Immunity''' and '''Wave Resistance''' do not work well with his relatively low health, as enemies with such abilities, even within his target traits, simply inflict too much damage for him to handle. '''Knockback''' is slightly better, but only against a select number of Red/Dark enemies with low knockback counts, making it pretty situational given the more effective counters available against them, as well as his ability being quite effective already.

===''' Ultra Talents'''===
Masamune has 4 Ultra Talents, all of which help him by quite a bit.

'''Mini-Wave''': Although this may seem small, Mini-Wave is amazing on Masamune, as it not only adds a flat 20% increase to his DPS when fully upgraded, but it also pairs incredibly well with his Knockback ability, pushing back Red and Dark enemies even further, including the few that normally outranged him. 

'''HP Buff+''': This brings his HP up to 204,800 without the extra 20% from HP buff; with the extra 20% it’s 245,760. This talent massively increases his survivability and is worth getting if you plan on getting his other Ultra Talents. 

'''Sage Slayer''': This talent improves several potential interactions, including against [[Sage of Logic Newtone]], though the application is still limited. One of his best uses against Sages is against [[Doctor K.O.]], as Date outranges them by a fair amount. He remains situational, but he isn't outright bad is as many scenarios with this upgrade. 

'''Savage Blow''': This Talent makes Masamune into a good source of generalist DPS, bringing his average DPS up to 23,514 with all his other Talents, which is just over twice as much as without any. Additionally, it means his Mini-Waves themselves can become fairly dangerous, offering excellent pierce to hit nasty backliners. However, in order for him to reach his full potential, you would need to spend a whopping 1,805 NP. So, at the end of the day, it may not be worthwhile to make such a hefty investment in a unit with an ability infamous for sometimes causing more harm than good.

